WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.100
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:04.580
“Adam was but human…

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:11.629
He did not want the apple for the apple’s
sake, he wanted it only because it was forbidden.”

00:00:11.629 --> 00:00:13.950
wrote Mark Twain.

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:26.400
Now I want you to do something for me, do
NOT think of a white bear for the remainder

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:31.720
of this video - oh, you've already failed
haven't you?

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:36.290
The reason you thought about a white bear
was the exact same reason you clicked on this

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:37.510
video.

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:41.970
This same instruction was given to a group
of test participants in the 80s.

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:48.030
They said, for the next several minutes, "whatever
you do, don't think about a white bear".

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:50.879
Of course, they all failed too.

00:00:50.879 --> 00:00:55.710
For the next several minutes all they could
think about was a white bear, no matter how

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:57.960
hard they tried not to.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:02.520
Many of them attempted to think of other,
random scenarios, picturing themselves on

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:10.080
holiday for example, to try to divert their
minds but a white bear always found its way

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:15.070
into their thoughts and before they knew it,
they were sky diving in Venezuela with a polar

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:16.070
bear.

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:20.330
At the end of the study they all admitted
that their attempts to not think of a white

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:24.070
bear were entirely futile.

00:01:24.070 --> 00:01:31.390
Why do our brains have a natural tendency
to think of or do the exact opposite of what

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:33.060
they're told?

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:36.230
Reverse Psychology can be very powerful.

00:01:36.230 --> 00:01:42.280
Today the middle and upper class in Europe
eat a diet that consists mainly of Kale Chips

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:47.230
and Hummus but in the 17th century they ate
potatoes.

00:01:47.230 --> 00:01:55.100
That's right, the humble spud, today a European
staple, was, for a long time only eaten by

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:57.540
the upper classes and royalty.

00:01:57.540 --> 00:02:02.970
The lower class were superstitious of the
potato, they saw it as bland, tasteless and

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:04.780
many thought it was poisonous.

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:11.030
But the upper echelons of society saw the
potential of the unassuming brown vegetable

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:12.860
and ate it plentifully.

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:18.920
During the period of the French revolutionary
wars, the usual food staples in England, which

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:25.160
was at the time basically some variation of
a meat pie, was in short supply and England

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:27.030
was on the brink of a famine.

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:32.190
So the English government took steps to try
to get the English public to eat more potatoes,

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:34.220
which were in plentiful supply.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:38.900
They went so far as to hand out pamphlets
entitled "Hints Respecting the Culture and

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:46.590
Use of Potatoes", but no matter how much they
pleaded with the people, they wouldn't eat

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:47.590
potatoes.

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:52.830
The same struggle to make potatoes a normal
food staple was happening across the whole

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:53.940
of Europe.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:03:01.510
Eventually it took someone to do something
quite different and not ask people to eat

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:05.090
potatoes, but to use reverse psychology.

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:08.100
Enter Frederick the Great of Prussia.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:13.440
The king of what is now Germany saw great
potential in the potato as a way to cheaply

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:18.490
feed the nation and not rely so heavily on
expensive bread.

00:03:18.490 --> 00:03:26.160
So, in 1774 he issued an order to his subjects
to start growing potatoes, to which they replied

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:31.650
"The things have neither smell nor taste,
not even the dogs will eat them, so what use

00:03:31.650 --> 00:03:33.100
are they to us?"

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:40.700
So he concocted a plan, he planted a grand,
royal field of potatoes and stationed royal

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:44.420
guards to protect the field every day.

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:49.660
The local peasants started to grow suspicious,
what food could be so valuable that it requires

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:51.890
round-the-clock guard protection.

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:57.910
And, just as Frederick had predicted, within
a few days the local thieves were stealing

00:03:57.910 --> 00:04:04.900
potatoes from the royal plantation and selling
them at the local market for a high price.

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:08.410
Before long the whole town was eating his
royal potatoes.

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:14.300
His plan had worked perfectly, because he
had made them forbidden and told people that

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:18.430
they can't have the potatoes, suddenly everyone
wanted potatoes.

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:25.330
And so, over the following years the fondness
for potatoes spread across Europe.

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:31.910
Whether it's thinking about white bears or
eating potatoes, humans love to do what we're

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:33.810
told not to do.

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:37.160
Children are the ultimate victim of reverse
psychology.

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:42.440
Tell a kid a hundred times to eat their broccoli
and they won't budge, but tell them they're

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:46.440
not allowed broccoli anymore and suddenly
it's their favourite food.

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:50.520
But why can our brains be so easily duped?

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:55.540
Why can we not resist pushing the red button,
why do we always want what we can't have,

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:59.730
whether it be our neighbour's sports car,
or wife?

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:03.600
We even do the opposite of what we tell ourselves
to do.

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:07.770
When you're about to give a speech to a group
of people and you tell yourself to be calm

00:05:07.770 --> 00:05:13.350
and not to panic the complete opposite happens
and you start violently shaking.

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:17.890
It seems at times that our brains are just
out to get us.

00:05:17.890 --> 00:05:19.120
Why?

